import{_ as a,o as r,c as t,a2 as o}from"./chunks/framework.BdWD-ld-.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"2026-11-18 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"2026-11-18 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence","outline":[2,3]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-18.md","filePath":"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-18.md","lastUpdated":1795079081000}'),i={name:"en/runtime/daily-intelligence/2026-11-18.md"};function n(s,e,c,l,d,p){return r(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="_2026-11-18-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" tabindex="-1">2026-11-18 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2026-11-18-agent-research-and-competitive-intelligence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;2026-11-18 Agent Research and Competitive Intelligence&quot;">​</a></h1><p>Core judgment: governance is becoming explicit data authorization, evidence-gated recovery, repeatable evaluation and cross-client audit. Multi-agent delivery also needs distinct child outcomes, result consumption and actual independent review.</p><p>Started 2026-11-18 10:05:23 Asia/Shanghai. Fresh main Registry: 47 people; 88 original repository entries, 264 first-page queries. Continue 2026-11-17T024823Z per-source baselines while preserving older gaps. Dates below are UTC. Merged does not mean released; local experiments, articles and development assignments: zero.</p><h2 id="factual-observations" tabindex="-1">Factual observations <a class="header-anchor" href="#factual-observations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Factual observations&quot;">​</a></h2><p><span id="o1"></span></p><h3 id="o1-adk-stops-implicit-session-state-disclosure" tabindex="-1">O1 ADK stops implicit session-state disclosure <a class="header-anchor" href="#o1-adk-stops-implicit-session-state-disclosure" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O1 ADK stops implicit session-state disclosure&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Committed November 17, breaking security change. MCP prompt arguments no longer implicitly select session-state strings by server-declared names. Only developer-supplied arguments are sent, none by default. Existing parameterized prompts require migration; this is not proof of a production leak.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/889ddd3134df1dd1a626205ee78811950dec2a5c" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o2"></span></p><h3 id="o2-openhands-distinguishes-post-send-gateway-timeouts" tabindex="-1">O2 OpenHands distinguishes post-send gateway timeouts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o2-openhands-distinguishes-post-send-gateway-timeouts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O2 OpenHands distinguishes post-send gateway timeouts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #6547. Post-send 504 carries X-Should-Retry:false and conversation ID; known pre-send timeouts remain retryable. The original run may continue and unkeyed manual resends may duplicate it. Upstream notes a missing complete base/head default-client comparison and an unrun credential-dependent live-model recipe.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OpenHands/software-agent-sdk/pull/6547" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o3"></span></p><h3 id="o3-paperclip-gates-preparation-recovery-on-execution-evidence" tabindex="-1">O3 Paperclip gates preparation recovery on execution evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#o3-paperclip-gates-preparation-recovery-on-execution-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O3 Paperclip gates preparation recovery on execution evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #22096. Transient preparation failures may continue after workspace recovery, only with preparing state, no provider execution evidence, released leases/stop receipts and verified repair. Generic adapter_failed still waits for a person. High learning value; recovery-governance competitive attention increases.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22096" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o4"></span></p><h3 id="o4-paperclip-reserves-disk-for-its-recovery-controller" tabindex="-1">O4 Paperclip reserves disk for its recovery controller <a class="header-anchor" href="#o4-paperclip-reserves-disk-for-its-recovery-controller" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O4 Paperclip reserves disk for its recovery controller&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #22068. Upstream describes 83 failed relaunches in seven minutes after a 10 GiB disk filled. A controller-owned reserve is released for recovery, with a named terminal cause when exhausted. Incident counts are upstream evidence. High learning value; track resource-exhaustion recovery.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22068" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o5"></span></p><h3 id="o5-paperclip-classifies-lease-transport-failures" tabindex="-1">O5 Paperclip classifies lease transport failures <a class="header-anchor" href="#o5-paperclip-classifies-lease-transport-failures" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O5 Paperclip classifies lease transport failures&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #22087. Daytona connection failures that lose errno become closed-set CONNECTION_FAILED diagnostics, using existing 30/60-second retries and the automatic-run brake. A wrong URL can also incur about 90 seconds of delay. High learning value with explicit retry cost.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22087" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o6"></span></p><h3 id="o6-paperclip-negotiates-relaunched-runner-compatibility" tabindex="-1">O6 Paperclip negotiates relaunched Runner compatibility <a class="header-anchor" href="#o6-paperclip-negotiates-relaunched-runner-compatibility" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O6 Paperclip negotiates relaunched Runner compatibility&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #21976. Optional capability negotiation reports the actual relaunched Runner build and accepts parked-state resume under upstream semantic-version compatibility rules rather than only the original digest. This does not prove arbitrary upgrade compatibility. High learning value; trial upgrade continuity.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/21976" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o7"></span></p><h3 id="o7-paperclip-makes-continuation-retry-keys-discoverable" tabindex="-1">O7 Paperclip makes continuation retry keys discoverable <a class="header-anchor" href="#o7-paperclip-makes-continuation-retry-keys-discoverable" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O7 Paperclip makes continuation retry keys discoverable&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #22046. A nested allOf hid required continuation fields in a Codex renderer; equivalent direct conditions expose retry keys while preserving canonical validation. Resolved account repair is also protected from stale failure reclassification. High learning value for model-visible versus enforced contracts.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/paperclipai/paperclip/pull/22046" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o8"></span></p><h3 id="o8-orca-preserves-human-wait-states-across-restart" tabindex="-1">O8 Orca preserves human-wait states across restart <a class="header-anchor" href="#o8-orca-preserves-human-wait-states-across-restart" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O8 Orca preserves human-wait states across restart&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #43474. Chats waiting for approval or an answer stay in the restart list instead of auto-running another model turn. Old approval requests are canceled; explicit resume creates a live request. High learning value and authority-recovery attention; retain second-circle placement.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43474" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o9"></span></p><h3 id="o9-orca-separates-unverifiable-ownership-from-mismatch" tabindex="-1">O9 Orca separates unverifiable ownership from mismatch <a class="header-anchor" href="#o9-orca-separates-unverifiable-ownership-from-mismatch" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O9 Orca separates unverifiable ownership from mismatch&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #43707. Unverifiable process identity reads retry within nine seconds, while definite mismatch ends proof. Restart concurrency is capped at min(6,cores). The ownership proof path excludes Windows; the cap applies across platforms. High learning value for observation versus identity failure.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43707" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o10"></span></p><h3 id="o10-orca-isolates-child-lifecycle-from-root-completion" tabindex="-1">O10 Orca isolates child lifecycle from root completion <a class="header-anchor" href="#o10-orca-isolates-child-lifecycle-from-root-completion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O10 Orca isolates child lifecycle from root completion&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #43672. Hermes child lifecycle hooks no longer complete the root conversation. Remembered child identities block delayed events from ending a newer root turn; child tool hooks show work only while the root is active. High learning value for multi-agent lifecycle adapters.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/stablyai/orca/pull/43672" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o11"></span></p><h3 id="o11-codex-bounds-cloud-stream-recovery" tabindex="-1">O11 Codex bounds cloud-stream recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o11-codex-bounds-cloud-stream-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O11 Codex bounds cloud-stream recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62151. Each replacement stream adds 500 ms delay; after three replacements the client errors while preserving transcript/draft. A stable 15-second connection or reset clears the count. This bounds reconnect loops, not execution effects.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62151" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o12"></span></p><h3 id="o12-codex-captures-accepted-outputs-before-later-inference" tabindex="-1">O12 Codex captures accepted outputs before later inference <a class="header-anchor" href="#o12-codex-captures-accepted-outputs-before-later-inference" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O12 Codex captures accepted outputs before later inference&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #61973. Accepted outputs retain order, identity and provenance even without a later inference request. Identical bodies with different IDs remain distinct, and local reset checkpoints are recorded. Audit captures acceptance rather than only model-visible snapshots.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/61973" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o13"></span></p><h3 id="o13-codex-snapshots-attribution-at-delegation" tabindex="-1">O13 Codex snapshots attribution at delegation <a class="header-anchor" href="#o13-codex-snapshots-attribution-at-delegation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O13 Codex snapshots attribution at delegation&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #62072. Children inherit the originating turn’s cost_center snapshot, unaffected by later parent updates. Selected override/request metadata is excluded and child IDs remain distinct. Attribution inheritance is not delegated authority.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62072" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o14"></span></p><h3 id="o14-codex-removes-yesterday-s-ssh-directory-special-case" tabindex="-1">O14 Codex removes yesterday’s SSH-directory special case <a class="header-anchor" href="#o14-codex-removes-yesterday-s-ssh-directory-special-case" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O14 Codex removes yesterday’s SSH-directory special case&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #62058. The empty read-only overlay on /etc/ssh/ssh_config.d and related documentation/test fixture are removed; configured filesystem policy now governs access. Yesterday’s O43 special masking mechanism has therefore been revised, not a stable current design.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62058" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o15"></span></p><h3 id="o15-codex-restricts-windows-sandbox-service-control" tabindex="-1">O15 Codex restricts Windows sandbox service control <a class="header-anchor" href="#o15-codex-restricts-windows-sandbox-service-control" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O15 Codex restricts Windows sandbox service control&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #62122. SYSTEM/elevated administrators receive full service control, other authenticated users limited query/start access. Startup fails if the ACL cannot be applied. Mainline status does not establish updated Windows installers.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62122" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o16"></span></p><h3 id="o16-codex-exposes-child-status-and-transcripts" tabindex="-1">O16 Codex exposes child status and transcripts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o16-codex-exposes-child-status-and-transcripts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O16 Codex exposes child status and transcripts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #62149/#62157/#62159. Spawn-tree agents and transcripts become navigable; completed/stopped/failed outcomes persist and live updates win over stale discovery. The value is observable collaboration, beyond a sidebar change.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62149" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o17"></span></p><h3 id="o17-codex-checks-resume-fork-endpoint-conflicts" tabindex="-1">O17 Codex checks resume/fork endpoint conflicts <a class="header-anchor" href="#o17-codex-checks-resume-fork-endpoint-conflicts" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O17 Codex checks resume/fork endpoint conflicts&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #62065. Conflicting root/subcommand remote endpoints fail before token lookup for resume and fork. This clarifies backend binding at an adapter boundary, not an FCoP routing standard.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/codex/pull/62065" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o18"></span></p><h3 id="o18-agents-python-0-25-ships-integration-changes" tabindex="-1">O18 Agents Python 0.25 ships integration changes <a class="header-anchor" href="#o18-agents-python-0-25-ships-integration-changes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O18 Agents Python 0.25 ships integration changes&quot;">​</a></h3><p>v0.25.0 published November 18 UTC with November 17 changelog date. It includes third-party session utilities, opt-in handoff recovery and concurrent MCP v2 HTTP requests, and removes the Runloop sandbox provider. Check provider dependencies before upgrading; the release is new, not every constituent merge.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/releases/tag/v0.25.0" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o19"></span></p><h3 id="o19-agents-python-normalizes-memory-timestamps" tabindex="-1">O19 Agents Python normalizes memory timestamps <a class="header-anchor" href="#o19-agents-python-normalizes-memory-timestamps" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O19 Agents Python normalizes memory timestamps&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 18, #6066. Consolidation compares timestamps in UTC with fractional precision, including existing raw memories, preventing selection caps plus different offsets from choosing an older rollout. Selection correctness is not cross-user isolation.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-python/pull/6066" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o20"></span></p><h3 id="o20-agents-js-approval-resume-proposal-is-now-merged" tabindex="-1">O20 Agents JS approval-resume proposal is now merged <a class="header-anchor" href="#o20-agents-js-approval-resume-proposal-is-now-merged" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O20 Agents JS approval-resume proposal is now merged&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #2673, updating yesterday’s O13 OPEN state. Resume evaluates completed sibling outputs in original order, emits/persists only newly completed results and validates restored receipts. No new npm release is established by this merge.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/openai/openai-agents-js/pull/2673" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o21"></span></p><h3 id="o21-claude-code-2-1-327-improves-credential-entry-and-recovery" tabindex="-1">O21 Claude Code 2.1.327 improves credential entry and recovery <a class="header-anchor" href="#o21-claude-code-2-1-327-improves-credential-entry-and-recovery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O21 Claude Code 2.1.327 improves credential entry and recovery&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 17. MCP JSON can be read from stdin to avoid tokens on command lines; status surfaces broken permissions/sandbox/hooks. Remote Control fixes deletion of running-session git-ignored files when stopping a worktree server. Release notes are upstream evidence, not local reproduction.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases/tag/v2.1.327" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o22"></span></p><h3 id="o22-langfuse-4-82-changes-audit-read-scope" tabindex="-1">O22 Langfuse 4.82 changes audit read scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#o22-langfuse-4-82-changes-audit-read-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O22 Langfuse 4.82 changes audit read scope&quot;">​</a></h3><p>MERGED November 17, #20045, included in 4.82. Audit reads move to ClickHouse with Event/Outcome. After project transfer the new organization sees post-transfer events only; list/export payloads differ, and duplicates can remain until background merges. Yesterday’s bulk-deletion audit merge is also included.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/langfuse/langfuse/pull/20045" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o23"></span></p><h3 id="o23-copilot-streams-activity-to-agent-365" tabindex="-1">O23 Copilot streams activity to Agent 365 <a class="header-anchor" href="#o23-copilot-streams-activity-to-agent-365" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O23 Copilot streams activity to Agent 365&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Official November 17 release streams cross-client Copilot session/prompt/response/tool activity to Agent 365 with Purview/Defender risk context. Available to Enterprise Cloud EMU customers. High enterprise-integration competitive attention; visibility does not establish universal pre-action enforcement.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-monitor-github-copilot-activity-through-microsoft-agent-365/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o24"></span></p><h3 id="o24-copilot-entra-authentication-enters-preview" tabindex="-1">O24 Copilot Entra authentication enters preview <a class="header-anchor" href="#o24-copilot-entra-authentication-enters-preview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O24 Copilot Entra authentication enters preview&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PUBLIC PREVIEW November 17, CLI 1.0.113+, Windows/macOS with Linux to follow. OIDC EMU SSO and Microsoft 365 inference/license access are distinct paths governed by different plans and policies. High identity/billing-boundary learning value; not universal zero-configuration access.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-copilot-cli-adds-microsoft-entra-sign-in-as-a-preview/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o25"></span></p><h3 id="o25-copilot-evals-offers-repeatable-customization-tests" tabindex="-1">O25 Copilot Evals offers repeatable customization tests <a class="header-anchor" href="#o25-copilot-evals-offers-repeatable-customization-tests" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O25 Copilot Evals offers repeatable customization tests&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PUBLIC PREVIEW November 17. Create repeatable checks for skills/custom agents/MCP, compare before/after customization, and approve each run. Uses local Vally with VS Code/CLI/App entry points. High trial value; not installed or proof of achieved reliability.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-copilot-evals-is-now-in-public-preview/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o26"></span></p><h3 id="o26-github-event-streams-offers-subscription-based-wakeup" tabindex="-1">O26 GitHub Event Streams offers subscription-based wakeup <a class="header-anchor" href="#o26-github-event-streams-offers-subscription-based-wakeup" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O26 GitHub Event Streams offers subscription-based wakeup&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PREVIEW November 17 with waitlist approval. A persistent connection subscribes to PR reviews, pushes, closure/merge and checks without a public webhook receiver. Useful event-adapter research; replay, disconnect recovery, ordering and exactly-once semantics remain unverified, not a same-layer FCoP replacement.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-event-streams-is-now-in-preview/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o27"></span></p><h3 id="o27-copilot-review-adds-risk-adaptive-effort" tabindex="-1">O27 Copilot review adds risk-adaptive effort <a class="header-anchor" href="#o27-copilot-review-adds-risk-adaptive-effort" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O27 Copilot review adds risk-adaptive effort&quot;">​</a></h3><p>November 17: adaptive effort, public-repository cross-repository context and secret detection enter public preview. Balanced remains default and Adaptive cannot exceed organizational maximum effort. Azure Repos review is GA. Study risk/cost and visible effort selection; detector quality was not independently tested.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-copilot-code-review-adaptive-effort-secret-detection-and-more/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o28"></span></p><h3 id="o28-copilot-app-adds-signed-in-browser-execution" tabindex="-1">O28 Copilot App adds signed-in browser execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#o28-copilot-app-adds-signed-in-browser-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O28 Copilot App adds signed-in browser execution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>November 17 browser use preview works via Chromium extension/isolated tab group, off by default with Computer/Browser Use opt-ins. Azure DevOps integration is preview without cloud sessions. GHES GA was already reported; today’s recap is scope context, not a second GA event. High product competitive attention around identity and sensitive-action approval.</p><p><a href="https://github.blog/changelog/2026-11-17-github-copilot-app-microsoft-ignite-releases/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o29"></span></p><h3 id="o29-eigent-1-0-8-integrates-work-logs-and-approvals" tabindex="-1">O29 Eigent 1.0.8 integrates work logs and approvals <a class="header-anchor" href="#o29-eigent-1-0-8-integrates-work-logs-and-approvals" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O29 Eigent 1.0.8 integrates work logs and approvals&quot;">​</a></h3><p>RELEASED November 17. Default work-log timeline links approvals/questions to files or commands and marks model changes; search spans tasks/files/automations. Included for delivery observability, not cosmetic navigation. Medium-high learning/product attention; no installation acceptance, radar circle unchanged.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/eigent-ai/eigent/releases/tag/v1.0.8" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o30"></span></p><h3 id="o30-onward-daily-build-changes-windows-updates" tabindex="-1">O30 Onward daily build changes Windows updates <a class="header-anchor" href="#o30-onward-daily-build-changes-windows-updates" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O30 Onward daily build changes Windows updates&quot;">​</a></h3><p>DAILY BUILD v2.1.0-daily.20261117.1 published November 17, not claimed stable. Windows updates download, checksum and unpack in background, then a windowless helper swaps installation directories. High delivery learning value; signing, failed-update rollback and real-machine upgrade remain unverified.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/OPPO-PersonalAI/Onward-Agent-Workbench/releases/tag/v2.1.0-daily.20261117.1" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o31"></span></p><h3 id="o31-beads-release-candidate-declares-one-way-migration" tabindex="-1">O31 Beads release candidate declares one-way migration <a class="header-anchor" href="#o31-beads-release-candidate-declares-one-way-migration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O31 Beads release candidate declares one-way migration&quot;">​</a></h3><p>PRERELEASE v1.4.0-rc.3 November 17; normal channels retain stable. Migration of older stores to schema 74 prevents older binaries reading them; rollback requires backup restore. rc.1/2 to rc.3 adds no migration. Multi-platform assets are not proof of tested acceptance on every platform. High migration learning value.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/gastownhall/beads/releases/tag/v1.4.0-rc.3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o32"></span></p><h3 id="o32-agentlas-separates-shared-facts-from-agent-preferences" tabindex="-1">O32 Agentlas separates shared facts from agent preferences <a class="header-anchor" href="#o32-agentlas-separates-shared-facts-from-agent-preferences" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O32 Agentlas separates shared facts from agent preferences&quot;">​</a></h3><p>STABLE-CHANNEL os-v1.2.99 November 17. Personal-life/time wishes become shared facts; preference describes one agent’s response behavior. Existing records are not relabeled. Engine accepts but does not persist boundary; desktop stores it. Medium-high learning value; verify cross-surface persistence rather than inferring support from schema.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/agentlas-ai/Agentlas-OS/releases/tag/os-v1.2.99" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o33"></span></p><h3 id="o33-yue-zhao-agent-config-clarifies-reviewer-dispatch" tabindex="-1">O33 Yue Zhao agent-config clarifies reviewer dispatch <a class="header-anchor" href="#o33-yue-zhao-agent-config-clarifies-reviewer-dispatch" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O33 Yue Zhao agent-config clarifies reviewer dispatch&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Committed November 17. Upstream reports three Codex-only rounds despite a both default. Instructions now declare the resolved reviewer set before dispatch and remove a conflicting second selection rule. Automatic expected-versus-actual dispatch checks remain future work; upstream review rounds are not local experiments.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/yzhao062/agent-config/commit/ee57b98eb93df6b820b4e92376a015ef7aef8414" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o34"></span></p><h3 id="o34-browser-use-narrows-its-secret-isolation-claim" tabindex="-1">O34 Browser Use narrows its secret-isolation claim <a class="header-anchor" href="#o34-browser-use-narrows-its-secret-isolation-claim" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O34 Browser Use narrows its secret-isolation claim&quot;">​</a></h3><p>README revised November 17: vault/domain-scoped credentials stay out of prompts/task text, but model-written Python can read secret values. The broad claim that agents cannot see credentials is removed. This clarifies a boundary, not a shipped isolation fix.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/browser-use/browser-use/commit/e9337176a22aacfb5e514c7755f1904e789982d9" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><p><span id="o35"></span></p><h3 id="o35-adk-refreshes-skills-at-script-execution" tabindex="-1">O35 ADK refreshes skills at script execution <a class="header-anchor" href="#o35-adk-refreshes-skills-at-script-execution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;O35 ADK refreshes skills at script execution&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Committed November 17. Skill refresh no longer writes environments during model-request construction; script execution refreshes the actual target sandbox. With revalidate_skills enabled, direct file reads before execution can still see old copies. Study per-session effective versions, not instantaneous synchronization.</p><p><a href="https://github.com/google/adk-python/commit/5f2f2279c9a29c473efb4dec151ba4b53e841cd9" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Primary evidence</a></p><h2 id="research-analysis" tabindex="-1">Research analysis <a class="header-anchor" href="#research-analysis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Research analysis&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="a1-recovery-starts-with-execution-evidence" tabindex="-1">A1 Recovery starts with execution evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#a1-recovery-starts-with-execution-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A1 Recovery starts with execution evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o2">O2</a> · <a href="#o3">O3</a> · <a href="#o4">O4</a> · <a href="#o5">O5</a> · <a href="#o8">O8</a> · <a href="#o9">O9</a> · <a href="#o11">O11</a></p><p>Supported: OpenHands blocks post-send retries, Paperclip requires pre-execution evidence, and Orca separates human waiting from active work. Unverified: whether local CodeFlowMu restart preserves these distinctions. Candidate: inject pre/post-send timeout, full disk and restart while awaiting approval; measure duplicates, waiting and recovery latency. Compare state/receipt/evidence at FCoP; budgets, leases and reserves belong to Runtime. Costs include fault injection and unknown outcomes. Topic: what evidence permits safe takeover?</p><h3 id="a2-enterprise-governance-extends-across-identity-audit-and-evaluation" tabindex="-1">A2 Enterprise governance extends across identity, audit and evaluation <a class="header-anchor" href="#a2-enterprise-governance-extends-across-identity-audit-and-evaluation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A2 Enterprise governance extends across identity, audit and evaluation&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o1">O1</a> · <a href="#o15">O15</a> · <a href="#o21">O21</a> · <a href="#o23">O23</a> · <a href="#o24">O24</a> · <a href="#o25">O25</a> · <a href="#o27">O27</a> · <a href="#o28">O28</a> · <a href="#o34">O34</a></p><p>Supported: Agent365 visibility, Entra identity, Evals regression and explicit MCP arguments address different layers; browser integration expands signed-in access. Unverified: an end-to-end pre/post-action control loop. Copilot Evals is a trial candidate after checking license, installation source, run approval and local-data scope. Compare CodeFlowMu role identity, credentials and audit separately; do not infer central authentication requirements for FCoP. Costs include enterprise setup, privacy and model use. Topic: can evaluation assert that a sensitive effect did not occur?</p><h3 id="a3-delegation-root-outcomes-and-independent-review-need-distinct-evidence" tabindex="-1">A3 Delegation, root outcomes and independent review need distinct evidence <a class="header-anchor" href="#a3-delegation-root-outcomes-and-independent-review-need-distinct-evidence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A3 Delegation, root outcomes and independent review need distinct evidence&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o7">O7</a> · <a href="#o10">O10</a> · <a href="#o12">O12</a> · <a href="#o13">O13</a> · <a href="#o16">O16</a> · <a href="#o20">O20</a> · <a href="#o29">O29</a> · <a href="#o33">O33</a></p><p>Supported: child hooks once completed the root, resolved reviewers can be skipped, and accepted outputs need never reach inference. Unverified locally. Candidate: research→synthesis→independent-review with late child completion, identical outputs/distinct IDs, parent steering and approval resume; compare requested versus actual dispatch, consumption and acceptance. FCoP can compare task/artifact/provenance; cost attribution is not authority inheritance. Costs are durable IDs and acceptance steps. Topic: prove that independent review actually occurred.</p><h3 id="a4-protocol-watch-event-wakeup-is-complementary-integration" tabindex="-1">A4 Protocol watch: event wakeup is complementary integration <a class="header-anchor" href="#a4-protocol-watch-event-wakeup-is-complementary-integration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A4 Protocol watch: event wakeup is complementary integration&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o6">O6</a> · <a href="#o7">O7</a> · <a href="#o17">O17</a> · <a href="#o26">O26</a> · <a href="#o31">O31</a> · <a href="#o35">O35</a></p><p>Supported: event subscriptions, Runner compatibility, rendered schemas and effective skill versions each have contracts. Event Streams is an external source, not a same-layer artifact-coordination replacement. Unverified: disconnect recovery, duplicates and semantic preservation. Candidate: replay duplicate/reordered/disconnected events offline, measuring consumption and explicit gaps without claiming upstream exactly-once. Costs include adapter persistence, compensation and migration. Trial Beads RC only on backed-up copies.</p><h3 id="a5-competitor-learning-centers-on-continuity-and-maintainable-delivery" tabindex="-1">A5 Competitor learning centers on continuity and maintainable delivery <a class="header-anchor" href="#a5-competitor-learning-centers-on-continuity-and-maintainable-delivery" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;A5 Competitor learning centers on continuity and maintainable delivery&quot;">​</a></h3><p><a href="#o3">O3</a> · <a href="#o4">O4</a> · <a href="#o5">O5</a> · <a href="#o6">O6</a> · <a href="#o8">O8</a> · <a href="#o9">O9</a> · <a href="#o10">O10</a> · <a href="#o28">O28</a> · <a href="#o29">O29</a> · <a href="#o30">O30</a> · <a href="#o31">O31</a> · <a href="#o32">O32</a></p><p>Judgment: study Paperclip continuity/upgrades, Orca human-wait/root-child state, Eigent work evidence, Onward delivery and Agentlas shared-memory boundaries separately, not as proof of overall maturity. Prioritize Paperclip fault recovery and Orca approval restart, then Eigent end-to-end delivery evidence. Onward needs real Windows upgrade/rollback evidence. High learning value; retain radar circles and track product/governance risks. None installed/tested; licenses/commercial boundaries were not exhaustively rereviewed and must be checked before trials. Installation, credentials and rollback belong to Runtime/product.</p><h2 id="cross-project-patterns-disposition-and-dual-source-limits" tabindex="-1">Cross-project patterns, disposition and dual-source limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#cross-project-patterns-disposition-and-dual-source-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cross-project patterns, disposition and dual-source limits&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A1/A3 are recovery/collaboration experiment candidates, A2 enterprise-governance trials, A4 complementary protocol references/experiments, A5 competitor trial ordering. None executed or automatically promoted to development.</p><p>GitHub first pages cover commits, Issues/PRs and Releases for every repository, with selected PR/commit detail reads. Full pages remain partial. TSA returns three API 404s; original Superset migration history remains pending, not shutdown/no-change evidence. Discussions, architecture/install/license and all 47 people’s social posts/replies were not exhausted. Non-GitHub checks opened Cursor changelog, MCP blog, Yue Zhao homepage, GitHub changelog and six November 17 official announcements. Cursor/MCP still lead with November 6/11, not new events. Two GitHub links are one source type. Preserve six governance researchers’ provenance: Mansura’s project is not the official AGENTSAFE artifact; bot activity is not personal involvement.</p><p>Deduplicated against yesterday’s report: O14 revises yesterday O43, O20 updates yesterday O13, O22 adds release/read-path status, existing GHES GA is not a second new event. Model-name marketing, content-free patches and cosmetic UI are not separate observations. CodeFlowMu/FCoP relationships remain locally unverified research judgments.</p><p>Only four permitted source files change; preserve homepage entry/layout/public snapshots and business lifecycle facts. Publication/live acceptance depend on local receipts and chat, not a pre-claimed success here. No external comments sent.</p><h2 id="november-19-addendum-carryover-from-november-17" tabindex="-1">November 19 addendum: carryover from November 17 <a class="header-anchor" href="#november-19-addendum-carryover-from-november-17" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;November 19 addendum: carryover from November 17&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The two pending experiments in the <a href="./2026-11-17">November 17 follow-up</a> were neither run nor carried forward in this day&#39;s research. This was a tracking omission. The newly numbered A2 and A4 on November 18 cover different topics and do not resolve the November 17 items.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>November 17 experiment</th><th>Status through November 18</th><th>Next verification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A2: side effects and Stop/timeout settlement</td><td>Not run</td><td>Interrupt before dispatch, after dispatch and after a lost receipt; compare actual side effects, Stop receipts and recovery decisions</td></tr><tr><td>A4: child-result consumption and formal acceptance by the parent</td><td>Only the root acceptance projection was tested; the full parent-child flow was not</td><td>Run a parent task with multiple child results and an independent reviewer; check the parent and artifact version, consumption and acceptance</td></tr></tbody></table><p>This November 19 addendum does not recast either experiment as completed on November 18. Both remain unverified; neither produces an article or development review yet.</p>',169)])])}const m=a(i,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
